window.EN={"1":"By the promise between Arion and Linoan, the \"Liberation Army\" withdrew from Tahra.","2":"As for the next objective,","3":"the Fiana Freeblades and the Magi Squad, who wished to liberate Munster first,","4":"and Leonster's surviving retainers and the Tahra mercenaries, who wished to liberate Leonster first,","5":"were split into two opinions, but in the end, also in order to move the army efficiently,","6":"it was settled that taking Leonster first was the realistic course.","7":"However,","8":"Leif would here once again be asked to make a new choice...","9":"Lord Leif, to come out on the northern highway, we must descend this pass to the west.","10":"Count Dorias, so you do intend to advance east along the coast.","11":"I believe we should descend the pass to the east and attack from the lightly defended south side.","12":"South of Leonster is the Melfiye forest region.","13":"Do you not know that forest is called the \"Forest of the Lost\"?","14":"Naturally I am aware of the difficulty.","15":"But for that very reason the Empire should be off its guard.","16":"For us, inferior in strength, making nature our ally is surely the basis of tactics.","17":"I am opposed.","18":"Our fight is being watched by Thracia... no, by all the people of this continent.","19":"It is not enough merely to win.","20":"It must be something that gives courage and strength to the people groaning under the Empire's tyranny.","21":"We should raise the flag of Leonster and advance openly from the front.","22":"The northern highway is Leonster's front door. A great enemy army lies in wait. Many soldiers will die.","23":"Naturally I am prepared for that. That is exactly why I wish for an honorable death.","24":"Honor?","25":"...Lord Dorias, this battle does not belong to knights alone.","26":"It is a nuisance to have your way of thinking forced upon us one-sidedly.","27":"August, is that not a somewhat insolent way to speak?","28":"...Well, never mind. It is Lord Leif who decides. There is no need for us to quarrel.","29":"Quite so. All shall be as the prince decides...","30":"Boss, we've found the perfect prey. Let's take that village today.","31":"Tch, what a run-down village. Even if we torch that, it won't amount to much of a haul.","32":"But there seem to be a fair number of young women.","33":"How about we catch 'em and sell 'em off to the slave traders?","34":"I see... not bad.","35":"All right, we'll catch just the young women and kill the rest.","36":"Well then, Father, please take good care of the children.","37":"Leave it to us. Even imperial soldiers should not reach as far as a poor village in mountains like these.","38":"We will protect the children in our care even at the cost of our lives.","39":"But Lady Amalda, will you be all right?","40":"If the Empire learns of this, will harm not come to you...","41":"I am ashamed.","42":"That as a knight of the proud House Friege, I can save children only in a manner like this...","43":"Every day, many children are captured and sent to the capital,","44":"and those I can save are no more than a tiny handful.","45":"I have meant to remonstrate with His Majesty the King, even if it should cost my life,","46":"and have requested an audience many times, but that has still not been permitted.","47":"As a general entrusted with an army, however unworthy, I agonize every day over what I should do.","48":"Lady Amalda, I well understand how you feel. But you must not be impatient.","49":"But, Father Sleuf, I...","50":"To lose you now","51":"would mean losing even the children who might be saved from here on.","52":"Yes... Thank you. Then I will take my leave...","53":"She, too, is in a painful position. Not that our own anguish is any different...","54":"Mm... But it is true that, at this rate, the world will be destroyed.","55":"Even knowing that, all we can do is pray...","56":"Father, at the Tower of Bragi, I truly heard it.","57":"\"When the three lights become one, the darkness of this world shall be dispelled.\"","58":"The voice of Father Claud, who is supposed to have died...","59":"Yes. And he also said this: \"Thou who art good, servant of Bragi,","60":"in place of me who cannot move, become thou my eyes, and see the world through to the end\"...","61":"I understand. You should set out on your journey. There is no need to worry about the children.","62":"Yes... Forgive me. Please pardon my selfishness.","63":"Father, trouble. Bandits are bearing down from the north.","64":"What, is that true?","65":"Yes, no mistake.","66":"The lady knight says she'll fight, but with just her and me, I don't know how long we can hold out.","67":"Father, take the women and children and get away.","68":"I see... Understood. Ralf, I'm sorry...","69":"That a mercenary of your caliber fights for a small village like this... everyone is grateful for it.","70":"Heh... This too is some kind of fate. Can't be helped!","71":"Oh, thank you for saving the village.","72":"I would like to thank your leader as well. Where might he be?","73":"Oh, thank you for saving the village.","74":"You have saved us.","75":"This is a token of the villagers' feelings. Please accept it.","76":"Then we'll be on our way...","77":"Where will you be going from here?","78":"East... We intend to head for Leonster.","79":"Then I have one request. A disciple of mine named Sleuf has set out on a journey.","80":"If you should happen to meet him, I would like you to call out to him, Lord Leif.","81":"Now, with this Warp staff, let me send you part of the way.","82":"As for the road to Leonster, there is the way out to the south of Leonster through the forest of Melfiye, the so-called \"Forest of the Lost,\"","83":"and the way of advancing east along the coast and crossing Fort Norden. There are these two.","84":"Which will you choose? → Fort Norden / Forest of Melfiye","85":"You people are strong. You look like you could handle this sword.","86":"I'll give it to you as thanks for coming to help.","87":"Hey, you folks, good timing. I'll give you this bracelet.","88":"Don't worry about it. Even if I kept it, they'd just steal it from me.","89":"Oh, you folks came to save the village? Much obliged.","90":"I'll give you this lance in thanks. It's a good one... supposedly, but I can't really tell.","91":"After all, I can't use it myself. Wahahaha...","92":"Hey you, what do you make of this scrap of paper?","93":"I picked it up on the road the other day, but isn't it kind of creepy?","94":"But I'd hate to throw it away and get cursed or something...","95":"Huh? You'll take it off my hands? Thank you, take it right away.","96":"If we pass north from here, we come out on the Leonster highway.","97":"The Empire's regular army lies in wait, and a difficult battle is expected,","98":"but is that acceptable? → Yes / No","99":"If we head north from here, we come out in a deep forest region called the \"Forest of the Lost.\"","100":"The enemy will likely be few, but unforeseen difficulties may await.","101":"Is that acceptable? → Yes / No","102":"Are you the village's mercenary?","103":"No, I don't recall taking any money from the village. Not that I'd want to take any from a village this poor.","104":"Then why for the village's sake?","105":"They looked after me on my travels, so I'm just lending a hand.","106":"You're a brat full of blunt questions. Who on earth are you?","107":"Ah, pardon me. I am Leif of Leonster.","108":"Leif? ...Oho... So you're Prince Leif.","109":"This is a good place to run into you. I'm a humble mercenary called Ralf. Would you let me join your army, Prince?","110":"Of course. For someone like you, I'd almost be the one asking.","111":"But why? Would you tell me your reason?","112":"Is \"I can't stand the imperial soldiers' tyranny\" not reason enough?","113":"Understood. That's enough.","114":"Mercenary Ralf, my wish is to liberate the people suffering under the Empire's tyranny.","115":"Can you swear to fight for that?","116":"Yeah, leave it to me!","117":"It seems that army will save the village. That's a relief.","118":"...I should be getting back to the army as well.","119":"Who goes there! A pawn of the Empire!?","120":"Nothing so boorish as that. If you don't want to die, don't point your sword at me.","121":"My Astra does not exist to cut down a little girl like you.","122":"Astra? ...Isn't that the technique said to be the secret art of the Isaachian royal family... Which means, could you be...","123":"Heh... You're quick on the uptake. That's right. I am Shannan, Prince of Isaach.","124":"But for certain reasons I am hiding my identity now. So forget that you met me and...","125":"Lord Shannan! I have a request!","126":"Whoa! Wh-what, so suddenly! You startled me.","127":"Please teach me the sword!","128":"Even a little is fine. If you could teach me just the barest touch of that Astra...","129":"......","130":"Please! I want to become strong! I want to become strong no matter what!!","131":"...Well, if it's just a touch...","132":"R-really? Please do!","133":"Hmm, this has gotten troublesome. Well, I'll bluff my way through and be done with it...","134":"With Astra, the technique itself matters, but what's important is the heart.","135":"Only when technique and heart become one does the path to Astra open.","136":"Technique and heart...?","137":"Mm. First, try swinging your sword.","138":"But how should I swing it... Could you show me an example once?","139":"Mmgh... N-no, true Astra can't be used unless you master it through countless attempts.","140":"Once you've seen the technique, you'd just run to imitating it. Yes...","141":"Is that how it is... Then I'll give it a try for now. Hah!","142":"No good. You haven't got it at all.","143":"Hyah!","144":"No, no. Your feelings are running ahead of you... Put your heart into the technique, your heart.","145":"...Man, I'm really just making stuff up...","146":"Put my heart into the technique... put my heart into the technique... Haaah!","147":"Huh, this is... it can't be...","148":"...No way...","149":"...No, it can't be. It couldn't possibly be done this easily. Isn't that right, Lord Shannan!","150":"Huh? ...Y-yeah, o-o-of course. Th-this can't be called Astra...","151":"I thought so... I nearly got the wrong idea.","152":"A-anyway, I've kept my promise to teach you just a touch. I'll be going now.","153":"Yes. Thank you very much, Lord Shannan!","154":"Put my heart into the technique, put my heart into the technique...","155":"What is with that girl~","156":"Keh heh heh.","157":"You're ten years too early to pick a fight with me.","158":"Guoh! D-damn it... gah..."};
